Why: Correct the Task Manager refusal reason with the user-approved RunAsInvoker evidence: it relaunches itself elevated even from a non-elevated start, so the helper could not read or move its window and that window would cover the user's work.

diff --git a/crates/platform-windows/src/tools/launch_focus.rs b/crates/platform-windows/src/tools/launch_focus.rs
index c5cdf4417..d856df883 100644
--- a/crates/platform-windows/src/tools/launch_focus.rs
+++ b/crates/platform-windows/src/tools/launch_focus.rs
@@ -79,8 +79,12 @@ impl LaunchForegroundGuard {
         self.reported_foreground.load(Ordering::Acquire)
     }
 }
-/// Task Manager always ends up elevated, even from a direct non-elevated
